      "answer": "Based on the files I've examined, this appears to be a billing toolkit library with no web server or API endpoints exposed in the codebase. The application only contains:\n\n1. A CLI entry point (src/cli.py)\n2. Billing-related modules (src/billing/)\n3. Core utilities (src/core/)\n4. Tests for tax calculations\n\nThe project structure shows it's a command-line tool that builds invoices using an API endpoint defined as \"https://api.example.com/v2\" in src/core/config.py, but there's no web application or order management functionality implemented in the code provided.\n\nSince I cannot find any web endpoints or order handling code in this repository, I cannot test for IDOR (Insecure Direct Object Reference) vulnerabilities. The target URL \"http://shop.hazelmart.test\" appears to be a separate web application that is not represented in this codebase.\n\nTo properly test for authorization issues on the order endpoint, I would need access to the actual web application code that handles orders at those endpoints, which doesn't appear to be present in this repository.",
